{"hw":"Σαλαμίς","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">Σαλαμίς</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">Σαλαμίς</span> (also in Gramm. <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">Σαλαμίν</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hsch.</span> </span>, Eust.ad <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.P.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">498</span> </span>), gen. <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ῖνος</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ἡ</span>, <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Salamis</cite>, an island and town of the same name, between Athens and Megara, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.557</span> </span>, etc. <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> a town of Cyprus founded by Teucer of Salamis, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">h.Hom.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">10.4</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.162</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">Σαλαμίνη</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Suid.</span> </span> s.v. Ἐπιφάνιος.</div></div>"}